{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773166010,"nonce":"Kxq9CSc3kTYUuT78J4fRyx8wC6w=","title":"CDE composite nodes: frontend ignores template_graph from registry — subgraph always empty","message":"CDE node types (CDE Standard, CDE Decay, CDE Anti-NF, CDE Hybrid v9b) have template_graph and template_ui_state populated on ComponentMeta in the registry. These are delivered to the frontend via the /api/components endpoint as ComponentDefinition.template_graph.\n\nHowever, the frontend enterSubgraph action uses SUBGRAPH_FACTORIES[nodeSpec.type]?.(nodeId, nodeSpec) ?? createEmptySubgraph(). CDE types are not in SUBGRAPH_FACTORIES and have no factory, so they always show an empty canvas despite the backend having a real template graph.\n\nFix: either (a) add CDE types to SUBGRAPH_FACTORIES using a factory that seeds from the component definition template_graph, or (b) make enterSubgraph check nodeSpec.params for a template graph from the registry before falling back to createEmptySubgraph.","files":null}]}